  "id": "magic",
  "term": "magic",
  "definition": "Magic, or illusionism, is a set of effects and techniques that deliberately creates the experience of an impossible or unexplained event. In psychology, it is useful for studying how attention, perception, expectation, memory, causal reasoning, and emotion shape the mind’s construction and misinterpretation of reality.",
